{"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s28CustomDebugStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s17CustomReflectableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/Se","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SE","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s30ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteralP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SH","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertex set is any set of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" values. The edge set is a set of ordered pairs of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices: self-loops are allowed, parallel edges are not."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot (none while the vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are the "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s "},{"code":"0..<n","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in order, each its own slot). Edges are kept in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, so an edge’s position in "},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"code":"0..<edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and a weight can live"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in an array beside the graph. Each slot has a row of the slots of its out-neighbors, a parallel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row of those edges’ positions, and a row of its in-neighbors; the rows of each kind share one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, so the graph makes a constant number of allocations however many vertices it has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(amortized, like "},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), and copying it copies a constant number of buffers. A hash table from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"slot pair to position (open addressing with a multiplicative hash, not "},{"code":"Dictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s SipHash)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"answers "},{"code":"contains(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in O(1) expected. A graph built in bulk from sorted edges (a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"condensation, a line graph, a named graph) builds that table on its first lookup or mutation,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in O(m), so a result that is only traversed never pays for it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Removing an edge is O(1): the last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each row","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. So","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex order, edge order and edge positions are unspecified and may change after a removal.","type":"text"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule"]]},"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AdjacencyList"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"AdjacencyList.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList.swift#L24"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:19AdjacencyListModule0aB0V","modules":[{"name":"AdjacencyListModule"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","title":"AdjacencyList"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/adjacencylistmodule\/adjacencylist"]}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/Neighbors"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init()","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(_:)-2unw2","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(_:)-6cbnw","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(adjacency:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListM